DESCRIPTION Multi-tool band: correlate GPU telemetry, serving-pod readiness, and scheduling state into one verdict.

DEFINE CONST QUESTION AS "Is the GPU inference path healthy end to end: GPU metrics, the model-serving pods, and the scheduler's GPU assignments all consistent?"
DEFINE CONST MAX_DURATION AS 480 seconds

ASSERT(POST to discussion endpoint returns 200 with conversationId)
ASSERT(SSE stream emits "thread_found" event within 30 seconds)
ASSERT(discussion completes with "done" event within MAX_DURATION)

ASSERT(at least 1 specialist contributes with signal=agree)
ASSERT(coordinator produces synthesis)
ASSERT(synthesis is non-empty)

# Reference-grounded quality: the deferred LLM judge (kubemoot-fitness crew) scores
# the synthesis against this ground truth on method and honesty, not specific values.
ASSERT(DEFER synthesis REFLECTS "Cross-checks live GPU metrics, the readiness of GPU and model-serving pods, and the scheduler's GPU assignments, and reports a single consistency verdict. The correct verdict is what the live state shows at the time of the question: which GPU worker nodes are Ready and advertising nvidia.com/gpu to Kubernetes, whether each ModelServer is READY and its serving pods Running, and which GPUs the scheduler has assigned. When all of these agree, the correct verdict is healthy and consistent. When a GPU node is NotReady, cordoned or offline (for example its GPU is lent elsewhere), or a ModelServer or serving pod is not Ready or Pending because of it, the correct verdict names that node and workload and says the path is degraded or partly unavailable, consistent with the evidence; reporting that truthfully is correct. Empty GPU telemetry at sample time means no active inference, not a broken path. Claiming Kubernetes is unaware of GPUs that it lists, calling a serving backend broken, a state the live data does not show, or reporting healthy while the live data shows an unavailable GPU path contradicts reality. No fabricated inconsistencies.")
